   As to your comment: S_NYMPH describes monsters which are nymphs --- 
i.e., water nymphs and mountain nymphs. It most certainly /does/ "work" 
to distinguish those monsters. However, your patch at the moment only
singles out water nymphs for special treatment, as I mentioned in my
earlier post, so S_NYMPH might not be what you want.

   However, if you're only looking for water nymphs, the easiest and
(IMHO, IMLE) most idiomatic way to find out whether a monster is a water 
nymph is simply

     if (mon->data == &mons[PM_WATER_NYMPH]) ...

